@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] public-documentation-content
These files MUST contain only reviewed public instructions and synthetic examples.
Credentials, private gateway API instructions, account/fleet state and operational
crash artifacts MUST NOT enter these pages. Unknown paths MUST NOT select other
priv files. Runtime user content MUST NOT be rendered as trusted documentation.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] public-command-examples
Every porsche fenced example MUST parse with the shared command grammar. The
command reference MUST derive from the same catalog used by the SSH gateway.
Unimplemented behavior MUST be identified until its runtime acceptance passes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product;security] public-browser-extension-installation
The browser extension guide MUST require explicit Overalls server configuration
and describe Chrome's unsigned developer installation and Firefox's temporary
installation. It MUST NOT imply browser-store publication or permanent unsigned
Firefox installation, or promise downloads when the deployment disables them.
